 ### MR-39 (Low): the headline median mixes countries without saying so
-- **Status: fixed** by [fix-mr-3](fix-mr-3.md) (2026-10-23, 99d5640): with pay in several currencies in view, the stats line's and Insights' median is the main currency's (the chart rows' rule) and says so: Amazon "$141K base pay median" (all 13,980, 803 converted) is "$149K base pay median (US)" (13,177; its Details: "It is the median of the 13,177 roles paid in the US; 803 roles paid in other currencies are left out"), and the tiles read "of 13,177 in the US". The chart's caption uses the same basis ("Median base pay $149K US"; `chart.js` `headPay`). Tests: test/fix-mr-3.test.js MR-39 ×3, e2e [MR-39] ×2.
+- **Status: fixed** by [fix-mr-3](fix-mr-3.md) (2026-10-23, 99d5640): with pay in several currencies in view, the stats line's and Insights' median is the main currency's (the chart rows' rule) and says so: on the integrated build (fix-viz-5's MR-28 rule already keeps minimums and shift pay out of the median), Amazon's "$149K base pay median" (all 13,045 base-pay ranges, 516 of them in other currencies, converted) is "$152K base pay median (US)" (12,529; its Details: "It is the median of the 12,529 roles paid in the US; 516 roles paid in other currencies are left out"), and the tiles read "of 12,529 in the US". The chart's caption uses the same basis ("Median base pay $152K US"; `chart.js` `headPay`). Google $183K → $199K (2,061 paid in the US), Microsoft $168K → $177K, Netflix $427K → $455K; Cohere's main currency is CAD ($253K → $281K, "(Canada)"); Apple, Scale AI and Shield AI pay in one currency and are unchanged. Tests: test/fix-mr-3.test.js MR-39 ×3, e2e [MR-39] ×2.
 - **Where:**
   - the stats line "$141K base pay median" (Amazon);
   - the chart caption "Median base pay $141K";
diff --git a/public/features/insights.js b/public/features/insights.js
index c81b44d..1def204 100644
--- a/public/features/insights.js
+++ b/public/features/insights.js
@@ -435,7 +435,7 @@ export function createInsights(container, { onFilter, headingLevel = 2 } = {}) {
   function stats(jobs) {
     const s = summaryStats(jobs);
     const enough = s.basisN >= MIN_SAMPLE;
-    // MR-39: "of 13,177 in the US" when the median is the main currency's (pay in several currencies in view).
+    // MR-39: "of 12,529 in the US" when the median is the main currency's (pay in several currencies in view).
     const where = s.basis ? payBasisPlace(s.basis).replace(/^paid /, '') : '';
     const tile = (label, value, note) => h('div', { class: 'msi-stat' },
       h('div', { class: 'msi-stat__label' }, label),
@@ -444,7 +444,7 @@ export function createInsights(container, { onFilter, headingLevel = 2 } = {}) {
     return h('div', { class: 'msi-stats', role: 'list' },
       // UX-53 / UX-61 (fix-phone-text): "of 2,781 with pay" (it read "of 2,781 salaried ro…" at 360). UX-55: a range is
       // written like the cards ("$188K–252K"), so the tile no longer cuts its number at 1440.
-      // MR-39 (fix-mr-3): "of 13,177 in the US" when the median is the main currency's (pay in several currencies in view).
+      // MR-39 (fix-mr-3): "of 12,529 in the US" when the median is the main currency's (pay in several currencies in view).
       [tile('Median base pay', enough ? formatMoney(s.median) : '—', !s.salaried ? (s.posted ? 'no base pay posted' : 'no pay published') : enough ? `of ${fmtCount(s.basisN)} ${where || (s.posted > s.salaried ? 'ranges' : 'with pay')}` : `too few with pay (${s.basisN})`),
         tile('Middle half', enough && s.p25 != null ? moneySpan(s.p25, s.p75) : '—', where ? `of roles ${where}` : 'of roles with pay'),
         tile('Pay published', formatPct(s.payShare), `${fmtCount(s.posted)} of ${fmtCount(s.total)}`),
diff --git a/public/viz/chart.js b/public/viz/chart.js
index 5f5179e..8c61876 100644
--- a/public/viz/chart.js
+++ b/public/viz/chart.js
@@ -311,7 +311,7 @@ function headPay(items) {
   if (!b.basis || b.basis === 'mixed' || !b.left) return all;
   return { ...all, median: b.stats.median, p25: b.stats.p25, p75: b.stats.p75, n: b.stats.n, basis: b.basis, basisLeft: b.left };
 }
-/** MR-39: " US" after the caption's median when it is one currency's pay of several ("Median base pay $149K US"). */
+/** MR-39: " US" after the caption's median when it is one currency's pay of several ("Median base pay $152K US"). */
 const medianBasis = (pay) => (pay?.basis && pay.basis !== 'mixed' && pay.basisLeft ? ` ${basisShort(pay.basis)}` : '');
 /** " in the US" after a median, "" when the row has no basis; "mixed" names its currencies. */
 const basisWords = (r) => (r.basis === 'mixed' ? ', several countries’ pay' : r.basis ? ` ${payBasisPlace(r.basis)}` : '');
